  \begin{equation}\label{prob2}
p(x) = \frac{a}{\pi (a^2 + x^2)}
\end{equation}
  with $a<0$.  

 with my question at part (d),  

 Calculate the probability distribution $P(X)$ of the average, $X$, of $M$ values of x, each drawn from the distribution of $p(x)$. 

